96","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/remix-run/react-router/issues/716","id":71346096,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcxMzQ2MDk2","user":{"login":"mjackson","id":92839,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92839?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson","html_url":"https://github.com/mjackson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjackson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-01-25T01:31:13Z","updated_at":"2015-01-25T01:31:13Z","body":"A location's `getCurrentPath` method should always return a _decoded_ path. Once we're inside the router, we don't want to worry about whether or not paths are URL-encoded or not. We just assume all paths are decoded. So removing the `Path.decode( ... )` from `getWindowPath` would break things.\n\nSimilarly, a location's `push`, and `replace` methods should always expect their path argument to be decoded since it's coming back out of the router. Thus, they need to `Path.encode( ... )` before handing URLs over to the DOM (i.e. `window.location = ...;`)\n\nThere was a double-encoding bug that I fixed earlier today in fe5ec395f98e1d063539dd2211b590dd0840de59. I'm not sure if it had anything to do with your use case, but you might try running your code on master to see if it still exhibits the problem.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","react