:56017,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"This line causes a URL parameter to be encoded in a non-reversible way: https://github.com/rackt/react-router/blob/v1.0.0-rc3/modules/PatternUtils.js#L170\n\nWe have an IIS server that doesn't correctly resolve URLs because of this behavior.\n\nThe change was introduced here: https://github.com/rackt/react-router/commit/d955d7a69052fd649b58d00bd75301a533f67e06\n\nI'd like to know the reason that this behavior was introduced, as it's somewhat unexpected. To quote @mjackson:\n\n> Apparently + is a special character in query strings, but not in the path portion of the URL. \n> https://github.com/rackt/react-router/issues/716#issuecomment-71346876\n\nI've not been able to find conclusive evidence in the [URI spec](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986), but considering that encoding and decoding should be symmetrical operations, this seems wrong. There is some discussion in this [Stackoverflow thread](http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2678551/when-to-encode-space-to-plus-or-20).\n\nExample:\n\n```\nvar placeName = 'Laguna Beach';\nvar uri = formatPattern('/place/:placeName', { placeName: placeName });\ndecodeURI(uri);\n// -> \"/place/Laguna+Beach\"\n// Expected decoded URI would be \"/place/Laguna Beach\".\n```\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/remix-run/react-router/issues/2407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/remix-run/react-router/issues/2407/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"oyeanuj","id":9633371,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzMzNzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9633371?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oyeanuj","html_url":"https://github.com/oyeanuj","followers_url":"https://api.git